# The credential fixture is generated by the corpus test and never committed.
#
# Gitleaks scans git history, so a plausible credential committed once is found
# by every future scan of this repository forever -- and by GitHub's own secret
# scanning, and by anyone who clones it. Excluding it by path does not help:
# the path filter applies to the working tree, and history is not the working
# tree. The only version that stays clean is the one that is never committed.
#
# testdata/corpus/.dragon.yaml sets scan_ignored_files, so being gitignored
# does not stop the corpus scan from seeing it -- which is exactly the
# combination this needs: uncommittable, but still scanned.
secrets/config.env
